.TH EITAAS 1 "August 2026" "EITaaS-Linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
eitaas \- diagnose and launch community AVD connections with smart-card redirection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B eitaas doctor
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas inspect-profile
.I FILE
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas smartcard status
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B eitaas connect
.I FILE
.RI [ --backend=BACKEND ]
.RI [ --clipboard ]
.RI [ --single-monitor ]
.br
.B eitaas certificates
.RI { fetch | inspect }
.SH DESCRIPTION
EITaaS-Linux is an independent community helper for diagnosing and launching
Azure Virtual Desktop connections through a compatible FreeRDP 3 client.
.PP
It does not disable certificate verification, request a CAC PIN, or install
polkit rules or certificate trust anchors during ordinary operation.
.SH SECURITY
Connection profiles must be regular files owned by the current user without
group or other permissions. Use chmod 600 on a downloaded profile before use.
Clipboard redirection is disabled unless
.B --clipboard
is specified.
.PP
Use
.B --single-monitor
to override profile-provided fullscreen, multimonitor, and span settings with a
single-monitor window. Profile-provided resolution and scaling behavior remain
active.
.PP
Never publish real RDP/RDPW files or authentication callback URLs. See the
installed SECURITY.md documentation for reporting guidance.
.PP
Connections require a live Microsoft Identity Broker or an SDL FreeRDP build
with WebView support. Terminal URL and callback authentication is refused.
.SH BACKENDS
The automatic backend preference is XFreeRDP, SDL, then native Wayland after
secure authentication capability is established. Every selected client must be
FreeRDP 3 with AAD and PC/SC support.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. One indicates completed diagnostics with unmet
requirements. Two indicates invalid input or an operation error. A connection
otherwise returns the FreeRDP child exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcsc_scan (1),
.BR pkcs11-tool (1),
.BR xfreerdp3 (1)
